--- answer ---
The fix is complete. I couldn't run the test suite (the sandbox policy denied `python3 -m pytest` and `pytest` isn't installed), but the change is verified by inspection and `git diff --check` passes cleanly.

**Cause:** In `rstrip`, the `cache` list holds trailing matching items to be discarded. But after a non-matching item flushes the cache via `yield from cache`, the cache was never cleared. So on a later non-matching item, those already-yielded items were yielded again — duplicating any `pred`-matching items that sat between non-matching items.

**Fix** (`more_itertools/more.py:2655`): added `cache_clear()` right after `yield from cache`, so each matching run is emitted exactly once and then reset.